-- 69 -- **`u64(a)` -- the integer conversion `SYNTAX.md` always promised and the reader never
-- let through.** The pass test for the «K3» §4.1 repair.
--
-- `dokumente/SYNTAX.md`:588 marks `primary` "G9: kein `cast`" and :656-659 gives the reason:
-- "a call whose path names a type IS the conversion -- the distinction is a name resolution,
-- not a syntax question." Until 2026-09-04 the reader refused the token before that rule
-- could ever apply (`P002`, reproduced against the unchanged checker in
-- `messung/K3-BEFUND.md` §4.1); no corpus site had ever needed one, which is exactly why a
-- form that was documented and unreachable could stand this long.
--
-- «K3»'s `test_func` needed two, on its two most ordinary lines: `(u64) ktime_us_delta(...)`
-- and `(u64) test_repeat_count`. This file builds the same shape from a `u32` counter, since
-- that is the width the reader actually widens.

module beispiel::umwandlung {

-- **A widening conversion, used exactly the way «K3» needed one.** `M1` gives the result the
-- FULL range of the target type rather than carrying the narrower source range through --
-- the same conservative answer this checker already gives float arithmetic that mixes
-- widths and an `opaque` carrier's hidden representation: a silent guess would be a promise.
--
-- The two conversions are combined with `|`, not `+`: the SUM of two full-range `u64`
-- values leaves the width (`M104`, correctly -- the checker cannot know the two halves stay
-- small), and this file is meant to check clean, not to re-demonstrate M1's own overflow
-- rule on a value this pass deliberately widened to its full range.
impl fn kombiniert(a : u32, b : u32) -> u64
    effects { pure }
    costs   <= 5 ops
{
    return u64(a) | u64(b);
}

}
